  "packageHash": "9tTL6DTQyiP8MkJ74IqPVQlPk1bSmSMTBuX8X2AA9ZSuDJ4pA9DUUuCCG07UVxcjgA/Vp13iiKJHAa7lfGX0mg==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 250134362,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/EggyStudio/BevyCSharp",
  "published": "2026-11-11T23:16:11.507Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "The library's projects pack as one package again, BevyCSharp carrying every project's assembly, the modules' and the bridges, and the pack job measures it against the size nuget.org takes before anything is kept or pushed.\nThe library's areas become projects of their own, each packed at one version and depending on those below it at exactly that version, with the flat package a game names depending on them all.\nThe library's files move by git into the folders of the areas' projects of the coming split, inside the one project, with the paths that name them and AGENTS.md's rows following.\nA norm test holds the library's areas in the layers of the coming split, reading what each file names of another from the built library and its portable PDB, each file placed in its area's project by a list.\nThe game of life starts swapping its sprite's image once its programs are ready, so the image its shot shows is the same however many frames a device holds while they compile.\nThe game of life says in its capture's log the steps it ran by its shot, its frame and the image it shows, so the runner says by how much its picture differs.\nThe feature test makes its screen-space light's and old screen's programs when the panel turns them on, and the soak gives its first frames twenty-five minutes and prints how long each step of its start took.\nA clock held for loads also stands still while a shader program compiles and its compute pipeline is built, so the game of life starts stepping at the same moment on any device, and its picture is taken again since its steps start three frames earlier.\nThe table of programs the render side reads moves into a module of its own with its code as it was, so the programs' file keeps within 800 lines as the next commit adds to it.\nA script is compiled against every assembly the library names as well as those the process has loaded, so it calls a member whose signature names a module's type, as Render.SetWeather does.\nThe asset data moves under the scenes, and every edge Core and the areas had up the plan's order moves with its type or goes through an area's plugin, so the projects hold no cycle.\nGlobal illumination's and the sky's members of Render and the world's spawn helpers become extension blocks, which the listing, the cheat sheet and the script host's compiler read as the types' own.\nEach area's console commands move into its folder, and the command attribute, the catalog and the host that lends a command the world move into Core, which every area stands on.",
